course: dictionary
lesson: 11199
title: Within: a limit or a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Within is a small word with a big job: it shows the edge of something. It means inside a limit, so you do not go past it. «Adding within 20» means every answer stays at 20 or below.
explain: Within can also mean inside a place or group. «The lost ball was somewhere within the school grounds» means it was somewhere inside the school's land.
explain: Look for the limit in the sentence. It may be a time, such as minutes or weeks, a number, or a boundary. Try swapping in inside or in less than, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Within means inside a limit, not going past it.
fact: «Within 10 minutes» means in 10 minutes or less.
fact: «Within weeks» means in a few weeks or less.
fact: Within can also mean inside a place or group, such as «within the school grounds».
fact: «Within reach» means close enough to touch or get.
exercise: «Adding within 20 is fun.» What does within mean here? | Under the table | *Inside a limit of 20, not going past it | Going past 20 on purpose | Only the number 2
exercise: «Telling a trusted adult usually makes a secret much smaller within weeks.» What does within weeks mean? | Long after many years | Never at all | Only on a Sunday | *In a few weeks or less
exercise: «The lost ball was somewhere within the school grounds.» What does within mean here? | *Inside the school's land | Far away from school | Above the school roof | Outside the school gate
test: «A snack within reach is one you can get easily.» What does within reach mean? | Miles away | *Close enough to get | Locked in a box
test: «A tsunami may follow within minutes.» How soon might it come? | After many years | Never | *In minutes or less | On a Tuesday
exam: «Within 20» and «within the rules» both use within. What is the one idea they share? | Being outside everything | Going past the edge | *Staying inside a limit or edge | Shouting loudly
